00:20:08.525 --> 00:20:10.167
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:20:10.167 --> 00:20:11.332
I believe in you.

00:20:11.332 --> 00:20:13.526
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:20:13.526 --> 00:20:15.929
and whatever your one word is.

00:20:15.929 --> 00:20:18.277
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:20:18.277 --> 00:20:21.860
(paper airplane whooshing)

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.417
- I think of mix tapes
as sonic love letters,

00:20:27.417 --> 00:20:30.667
and I think a lot of my creative energy

00:20:33.185 --> 00:20:36.935
in high school was
literally making mix tapes

00:20:38.014 --> 00:20:41.152
to girls I liked, for friends of mine who

00:20:41.152 --> 00:20:43.410
I wanted them to get to know who I was.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:46.555
It was easier for me
to say this 90 minutes

00:20:46.555 --> 00:20:50.948
on this Maxell cassette
tape defines who I am.

00:20:50.948 --> 00:20:52.401
And the difference between a mix tape

00:20:52.401 --> 00:20:55.803
or a mix CD or a data CD
or whatever they have now,

00:20:55.803 --> 00:20:58.137
is that you have to listen
to it consecutively.

00:20:58.137 --> 00:20:59.472
So I'm taking you on a ride.

00:20:59.472 --> 00:21:01.045
I'm going to start with
a high-energy song.

00:21:01.045 --> 00:21:02.362
I'm going to switch it
up, and I might put in

00:21:02.362 --> 00:21:03.887
a funny interlude from
like an Adam Sandler

00:21:03.887 --> 00:21:05.176
CD or something.

00:21:05.176 --> 00:21:07.110
And then I'm going to hit
you with, my fourth song's

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.239
always the most important.

00:21:08.239 --> 00:21:10.439
That's the one that tells
you who I really am.

00:21:10.439 --> 00:21:11.965
- [Charlie] The fourth?

00:21:11.965 --> 00:21:13.492
- The fourth one, it's batting cleanup.

00:21:13.492 --> 00:21:16.492
It's literally fourth in the lineup.

00:21:18.767 --> 00:21:20.540
I think I still build scores the way I

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.284
used to make mix tapes for girls.

00:21:22.284 --> 00:21:23.941
I'm thinking of, okay, we've been in this

00:21:23.941 --> 00:21:25.996
energy for a while, now
I got to wake you up.

00:21:25.996 --> 00:21:28.497
All right, now we can
afford to sit in a ballad

00:21:28.497 --> 00:21:29.604
for a little while.

00:21:29.604 --> 00:21:32.424
And so when I read Ron's
book, and I started

00:21:32.424 --> 00:21:34.292
thinking about it, I thought of it the way

00:21:34.292 --> 00:21:37.433
I thought of making mix
tapes for my friends.

00:21:37.433 --> 00:21:39.228
I'm going to take you on this ride,

00:21:39.228 --> 00:21:40.685
and the ride's going to happen to tell

00:21:40.685 --> 00:21:41.765
you the story of this man's life.

00:21:41.765 --> 00:21:43.669
- And the first step is to draw you in?

00:21:43.669 --> 00:21:44.850
- Yes.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.249
The first song on a
mix tape is everything.

00:21:47.249 --> 00:21:49.705
It depends whether you,
if you fast forward

00:21:49.705 --> 00:21:52.404
through the first song, you messed up.

00:21:52.404 --> 00:21:53.237
Right?

00:21:53.237 --> 00:21:55.065
You're not going to press play.

00:21:55.065 --> 00:21:57.467
When you get a good
role, like, I'm not tired

00:21:57.467 --> 00:21:59.762
of playing Hamilton.

00:21:59.762 --> 00:22:02.236
I mess up in a new place every night.

00:22:02.236 --> 00:22:03.887
I get one certain part
better than I've ever

00:22:03.887 --> 00:22:05.138
gotten it every night.

00:22:05.138 --> 00:22:09.216
I think I will be revisiting
it for the rest of my life.

00:22:09.216 --> 00:22:11.724
But it's no accident
the best idea I ever had

00:22:11.724 --> 00:22:13.180
happened on vacation.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:17.638
So that's important, too,
as Arianna Huffington knows.

00:22:17.638 --> 00:22:19.197
Resting is just as important,

00:22:19.197 --> 00:22:20.952
and I always knew I'd do a year.

00:22:20.952 --> 00:22:24.452
I did a year when I was in In the Heights.

00:22:25.509 --> 00:22:29.174
That's my capacity, and then I can let

00:22:29.174 --> 00:22:31.164
other ideas into my brain.

00:22:31.164 --> 00:22:34.172
♫ And I am not throwing away my shot

00:22:34.172 --> 00:22:37.056
♫ I am not throwing away my shot

